    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d463-a1">

                <pb facs="0696" n="584" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg584"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Doctor Gore to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Philadelphia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-03-03"><hi rendition="#italic">March 3,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Will you kindly advise me whether it
                    would be necessary for one holding a diploma of the University of Pennsylvania
                    and a certificate of the state board of dental examiners of Pennsylvania to
                    undergo an examination in order to practice the profession of dentistry in
                    Athens, Greece.</p>
                <p>A prompt reply will be appreciated by,</p>
                <p>Yours, truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. J. Gore, D. D.
                    S</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
